From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:20:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: csid-340: Widen the PHY select field
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The PHY select field of CSI2_RX_CFG0 is three bits wide, bits 20 to 22,
as the vendor driver's csi2_rx_phy_num_mask of 0x7 says for both the
CSID 530 and the CSID 640. Two bits were enough for the two PHYs of the
QCM2290, but not for the fourth PHY of the SM6450, which is selected
with 4.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
index 023198574..199cf4a94 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 #define CSID_CSI2_RX_CFG0					(0x100)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_NUM_ACTIVE_LANES_MASK	GENMASK(1, 0)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_DLX_INPUT_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(17, 4)
-#define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(21, 20)
+#define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(22, 20)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_BASE_IDX	1
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_TYPE_SEL		BIT(24)
 
